[{"id":"VRCE-6-12-1","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":12,"verse":1,"english":"Hearing those words of the Wind-god's son, the irrepressible Rāma, conversant with all the Šāstras, replied, with words expressing his own opinion.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-18-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6012001","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1d97c2f2e9f6643624a13910c2e5e7f5e3f0f359f3567eef09b9cfb2ab6bdcf4","compact":"f0fc49a901580d5397c47a99482aaaffbcb87559a962bc8244f16fee5c04773b","nasal":"366344e5e23050c0d1097baee1e5b96a8893b05a04c6b29c035e8190e56ef264"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-12-2","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":12,"verse":2,"english":"I have also thought of some thing regarding Vibhisana. I wish you all, interested in my wellbeing, to hear that.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.778,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-18-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6012002","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"34e68a6a8c48147a546d3b659b919b1fc955d9fff3c683432b4bcc45229bfa8b","compact":"b19e9ad43c9e4be5479b12d625c2f53028a4d5285e0beb641477a42b977b696d","nasal":"b19e9ad43c9e4be5479b12d625c2f53028a4d5285e0beb641477a42b977b696d"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-12-3","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":12,"verse":3,"english":"(Vibhīşaņa) has come here as friend so I cannot forsake him by any means. And even if he has come with any evil intent it is not culpable for the pious to afford him shelter.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-18-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6012003","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a13583ec4f819bb0600a56a52a7cc6b998fd5ea06bfabc9267dbaa8c3c0fa45a","compact":"92af89c24c09dea1e3e109ea3c65dd4d31656b41e03f23635510bdf12ca7bc36","nasal":"92af89c24c09dea1e3e109ea3c65dd4d31656b41e03f23635510bdf12ca7bc36"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-12-4","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":12,"verse":4,"english":"Hearing the words of Rāma, Sugriva, the lords of those who go bounding, over-flowing with friendliness, bespake Kākutstha.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.691,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-18-33"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6012004","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ddea8817ae6d0546b4781beac4b1b1ce8f8b39a3775386da94593b772e06c4ac","compact":"0395267057bb701679f10db1625cad98e3a1d17a69eb263adaf8328dbd022891","nasal":"0395267057bb701679f10db1625cad98e3a1d17a69eb263adaf8328dbd022891"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-12-5","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":12,"verse":5,"english":"What wonder is there that you wouldst speak these auspicious words, O you the foremost of kings, conversant with morality, gifted with prowess and ever treading the pious track as you are.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.776,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-18-34"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6012005","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5088c7775ce8f14a756a7e227322937931b7a7e67f22c5a377a54c901a1680d8","compact":"46b95b76d008d7e59276e9bc21d6a69a6b1ca09edb40167307bfa6ce7d7a0ad0","nasal":"46b95b76d008d7e59276e9bc21d6a69a6b1ca09edb40167307bfa6ce7d7a0ad0"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-12-6","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":12,"verse":6,"english":"Truly does my inner self regard Vibhīşana as devoid of any wicked intention. He has been well sounded by signs and gestures.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.769,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-18-35"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6012006","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"071438163e344b4052be8a50254f9a45091f35ca41436b71ed3b4b3067e28e1c","compact":"f6aa8da03a18a890ecd7686ca74cce0f81d9c1f469af08466d0dd9b139db8111","nasal":"87fcdb70948580b1da06ed3f763061e023a24b38bfcc1151ec9c69a988508dba"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-12-7","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":12,"verse":7,"english":"And let the greatly wise Vibhīşaņa, O Rāghava, be placed on an equal footing with us and gain our friendship.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-18-36"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6012007","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4f8be35e7d8bf2f803843659c1f59caa6723eddc5304b975101d08141ceb08e0","compact":"3a4b616d8b04e0d293a1874dfcc7abf0d31d1a992f2c15fc9ef598a5bdc723b8","nasal":"3a4b616d8b04e0d293a1874dfcc7abf0d31d1a992f2c15fc9ef598a5bdc723b8"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-12-8","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":12,"verse":8,"english":"Hearing the words of Sugrīva, and weighing them, Rāma again addressed the foremost of monkeys with more reasonable accents.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.919,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-18-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6012008","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"beedf38ce5521c22079aea9e1b9b34130fd44f9bf32d331605c0beb5fd5467b1","compact":"c845d0e16fef318bb02b0484721b47596f82ef39bd8e1fb1f426b57228c9986d","nasal":"c845d0e16fef318bb02b0484721b47596f82ef39bd8e1fb1f426b57228c9986d"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-12-9","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":12,"verse":9,"english":"Wicked or other wise, whatever this nightranger may be, he shall not be able to do me the least mischief.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.833,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-18-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6012009","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d93567ea5fae4e105098c3ceac3bf52f95903950e5dc9bb1c1e836c0a53f256f","compact":"48fda721cd309da681c435bb7b9e21708d849c9ef962a7e16bd2971342c3b284","nasal":"48fda721cd309da681c435bb7b9e21708d849c9ef962a7e16bd2971342c3b284"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-12-10","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":12,"verse":10,"english":"Piśācas, Dānavas, Yakşas or all the Rākşasas on earth, I can slay them all, if I like, with the tips of my fingers, O you the lord of monkeys.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-18-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6012010","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e19e9345579d549c75ff01b00ad2d0cfb5ee57161ebf585b585bf654a0ec803d","compact":"ca470a57970048f6b7fd42896d04c6d4a594703e1042ccccd584f67d59f8f6e9","nasal":"835f8d881c348ce0706c21f9c900e6a1baf7b3ccc20a23c9329011d113e10101"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-12-11","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":12,"verse":11,"english":"I have heard of a pigeon adoring and entertaining with its own flesh, an enemy who took its shelter.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.815,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-18-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6012011","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"728e98e36ef4f10ed03db7cb60cf2039d77c0ac37794f3a85cc8eb72ca8f9a05","compact":"3e5534faa38041e6daebd3c1ec4cfb459903a23ea3ae61ba08e5e433fdd4ea55","nasal":"73484116490442fbb089f0f545a519e929411bb0be584ec21be1394ea242def4"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-12-12","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":12,"verse":12,"english":"While a pigeon received so friendly its enemy, the slayer of its mate, how can I then act otherwise, O foremost of the monkeys?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-18-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6012012","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1b8cb714aba767e00f4823ceb0072173943b8021fefe642b95256d9029cad2c4","compact":"ea1471dae19e078bd6ace2d11be8b26f02453ed34eb5096a9e59b43312e673b0","nasal":"ea1471dae19e078bd6ace2d11be8b26f02453ed34eb5096a9e59b43312e673b0"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-12-13","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":12,"verse":13,"english":"Do you hear, I shall relate, a sacred story, narrated by the great ascetic, the truthful Kandu, son of the ascetic Kanyā.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.631,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-18-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6012013","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"010caa31fc9cca1b26e6087d4e5088aecc3308365ec0edd49b4887a053aa3e57","compact":"713c7f3e61d8b13b87157063a15149f4ee46851c295b64727e31ac08b00d4f57","nasal":"9ebc8dd5bd5250cbc295183ffb14b5c7a2cdac57a23be42e3458af12d330b480"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-12-14","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":12,"verse":14,"english":"o slayer of foes, even a wicked-minded enemy, if he, with folded palms and a poor heart, crave for your shelter, should not be slain.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.898,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-18-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6012014","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c46332fc1b61bf4d7c010c571da2fa516af22efcb4bc052a4cfbd437522fde87","compact":"ec40b0f03f1f9b959aad69317adcccc27be69f76a235dee0dd40087abe7f476a","nasal":"f3544becb39e36db5c72295ab02c0ea231b08a654fbcaccf39a2c72fdbaef5da"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-12-15","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":12,"verse":15,"english":"If an enemy, proud or terrified, seek shelter in affright, he should be saved by a great man even at the risk of his own life.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.922,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-18-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6012015","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f06943e323fe936ac4a650dba3ce0ed6c30e3313862a8d9e4dd7ae5b8db72042","compact":"9f739b08b3df844c54aa7430310d3c83632903b0efd46df755e1a38376eb1f9b","nasal":"9f739b08b3df844c54aa7430310d3c83632903b0efd46df755e1a38376eb1f9b"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-12-16","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":12,"verse":16,"english":"One, who from fear, ignorance or wilfully does not protect him who seek his shelter, perpetrate a mighty iniquity, blamed of all.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.729,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-18-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6012016","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fdc47bde29eb5a539482f9ec663bd22178d02acd40936163d3deba9345dce17c","compact":"6bee18a8d4e9d23a3cebbba0f5dec58511fe61a5f4018df0dfe4aa63bf47c240","nasal":"6bee18a8d4e9d23a3cebbba0f5dec58511fe61a5f4018df0dfe4aa63bf47c240"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-12-17","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":12,"verse":17,"english":"When a person is slain before him whose shelter he has taken he take away all the virtues of his protector.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.86,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-18-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6012017","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7907df4463b4cc9b3f1afc0b57b6e52e08c7af89140524d7a39af2c674aec9d0","compact":"7a1d09d99304459081d0a043aa561aaaef6212b210d6bb6f586c0a3367e1b091","nasal":"7a1d09d99304459081d0a043aa561aaaef6212b210d6bb6f586c0a3367e1b091"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-12-18","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":12,"verse":18,"english":"So great is the sin in not affording shelter to those who seek for it; it stands in the way of going to heaven, brings in calumny and destroys the strength and prowess.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.81,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-18-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6012018","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f10a3da7461dd5339b6e041d15540fffe26e8cd36def09ee9f28a9778e61c13a","compact":"38918c5f7b8f63ff480f2b5b44fc10d868e739335fe77d8a13a53494df34577e","nasal":"8e716bfdc6176b8eca8c4d5729e59ff076f91fa0b18140fa3cce8cc455e7402f"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-12-19","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":12,"verse":19,"english":"I shall therefore follow the excellent words of Kaņdu-leading to piety, fame and the attainment of the abode of the celestials.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.841,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-18-30"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6012019","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d139850cff3a667f5e57bd8041cdb7de526fb8267cddec50ca4bdaad36974739","compact":"63c04d6543cffc6e0cb2811852c5fa4f048c9f23aa50b74775c43afc7ee19b58","nasal":"0b2b5d05189e8adc3e644fbee827a56eb9174b710a4226fafb023db8d60e78df"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-12-20","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":12,"verse":20,"english":"I always declare 'no fear' to all creatures, whenever any, approaching me, says, 'I am thine' and seek my shelter. Even this is my pious observance.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.875,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-18-31"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6012020","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2b5c88f54c938363a8a3bf5a27095770441d98f8b1699c26d5dea9a64b568dcb","compact":"bd260976ff2ee5e8109455c3ed32bde5ac519a9b51f968072c28cdeb64fbd2e5","nasal":"a27311b15cf77bb86c21e334de7c9c641ea91c676176b00aa5d8d5a38d595e4d"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-12-21","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":12,"verse":21,"english":"O Sugrīva, O foremost of monkeys, do you soon bring him here, whether he be Rāvaņa or Vibhisana and I shall declare to him 'no fear'.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-18-32"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6012021","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"41cf097665cd4f5ee3f7ca1e55f09e6de064ba3933026540f6256617b4526150","compact":"6f6c257ba00a8b127f6f47d309c655696d8d961f94edcbdc1bd0e676b7c47e37","nasal":"6f6c257ba00a8b127f6f47d309c655696d8d961f94edcbdc1bd0e676b7c47e37"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-12-22","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":12,"verse":22,"english":"Hearing the words of Sugrīva, the lord of monkeys, the king of men (Rāma) made instantly friends with Vibhīşaņa, like to the conqueror of enemies' cities making friends with the king of birds.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.892,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-18-37"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6012022","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8d6cbb1552de3ed51186fd580312d90979881deebdb2a29345408ed01c8c8ff3","compact":"145204d2b81c265e5b15642de4cfae20440053557ba435cb3c7e8936e5a245b8","nasal":"145204d2b81c265e5b15642de4cfae20440053557ba435cb3c7e8936e5a245b8"}}]
